# Corpus for the link census (Phase 0 of docs/link-build-plan.md).
#
# The three documents in src/eval/corpus/ are hand-written fixtures for the
# SEGMENTATION benchmark: a few hundred words each, fourteen anchors between
# them, and every one of those anchors a table-of-contents fragment. They are
# the right corpus for asking whether the parser finds a section boundary and
# the wrong one for asking how many references a page carries. A census run
# over them reports a median of zero outbound and passes G0 on no evidence.
#
# So the capacity gate runs over real pages instead. `npm run census:fetch`
# downloads these into src/eval/link-corpus/ (gitignored — the list is what is
# reproducible, not 3 MB of someone else's HTML), and `npm run census:real`
# measures them.
#
# Selection, and why each is here:
#
#   • Five Wikipedia articles. The design doc's "median 13, p90 25" came from
#     five Wikipedia articles, so the corpus that tests the claim has to
#     contain the class of document the claim was made about — and a
#     Wikipedia article is the densest reasonable case, with a real
#     bibliography, superscript citations, and a navbox at the foot.
#   • Two MDN pages. Reference documentation: heavy same-site cross-linking,
#     a sidebar of navigation, almost no external destinations.
#   • Two specs. Long, deeply self-referential, near-zero off-site links —
#     the low-outbound end of the range.
#   • One project README rendered by GitHub, and one plain long-form essay:
#     the ordinary web, where most pages actually live.
#
# All eleven are permissively licensed (CC-BY-SA, CC-BY, W3C/WHATWG document
# licences) or public technical documentation, and all are fetched read-only,
# once, for a local benchmark.
#
# One URL per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.

https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypertext
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spatial_navigation
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_reality
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_architecture
https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vannevar_Bush

https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebXR_Device_API
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Accessibility/ARIA/Roles/landmark_role

https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/
https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html

https://github.com/immersive-web/webxr
https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ten-usability-heuristics/
